ChannelsPage.tsx is a thin wrapper: `usePageTitle('Notification channels')` + a
`<PageContainer title subtitle copyLink>` whose only child is `<NotificationChannelsView/>`.
The manifest record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:notifications/Channels) extracts
exactly the page-level surface: NO dataSources, NO named panels, NO charts, NO maps, and the two
i18n strings `notifications.channels.title` / `notifications.channels.subtitle`
(requiredCount=2). The actual delivery-channel CRUD body is the *separately-shipped* feature view
`feature-views/NotificationChannelsView` (its Apple parity unit is already DONE — its files live
in apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/NotificationChannelsView.*). Faithful, non-narrowing parity
(covenant #2/#5) therefore = reproduce the PageContainer chrome (title + subtitle + copyLink) AND
host the real NotificationChannelsView (DRY — no re-implementation), driven by the page model's
NotificationChannelsModel. This is the identical structure the sibling page:notifications/Webhooks
(P7) used to host its WebhookChannelsSection — followed verbatim here.

