The value-less AppRoute enum's `.notifications` host is owned by the alerts inbox, and
/notifications/channels is a sibling alerts surface. Mirroring the sibling AlertRulesRouteRegistration
(same directory, same pattern), the native shell models it as a typed NavigationDestination: a host
stack adopts `.channelsDestination()` and pushes a `ChannelsLink` to open it. No AppRoute enum
widening is needed — AppRouteParser.parse("/notifications/channels") already resolves to
`.notifications` via its generic first-segment fallback (verified: firstSegment "notifications" ->
AppRoute.notifications.pathSegment). The copy-link share URL uses the canonical web path
"/notifications/channels" (a constant, not user-facing prose). Changes therefore stay entirely within
the allowed feature dir + catalog + ledger + this log (no Sources/App or TeslaSyncApp edit).

