    row, the Add Channel action, the add/edit form sheet, the per-row test/toggle/delete, and the toast.
  - Charts/maps: none (web source has none) — N/A.
  - 3 data states: the page's own surface has NO API data source (manifest declares none — it renders
    from navigation/local state); the hosted NotificationChannelsView owns + renders loading / empty /
    error (+ the orthogonal stale/offline connectivity axis) for its useNotificationChannels +
    useNotificationStats sources — its own parity unit, reused not re-implemented (DRY). The page's three
    previews (Loaded / Empty / Error) drive those states through the in-memory source.
  - Live data / staleness: handled inside the hosted section (its NotifChannelsConnection .stale/.offline
    freshness chip + banner + guarded auto-refresh, ADR-013).
  - i18n: the two visible page strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings by the web key names
    (notifications.channels.title / .subtitle) via the model's LocalizedStringKey; English fallbacks =
    the web t(key, default) second argument verbatim (ADR-014). Zero hardcoded user-facing literals.
  - Units: N/A — channel metadata (kind / name / enabled / masked config) is unit-agnostic control-plane
    data; no SI physical quantity crosses this surface (ADR — SI converter boundary not exercised).
  - a11y: header accessibilityElement(.contain); CopyLinkButton + the hosted section carry their own
    labels/traits; Dynamic Type via Font.TS roles + .teslaSyncTheme(); light/dark + high-contrast via the
    Color.TS dynamic tokens; ≥44pt controls from the shared TSButton (ADR-015). SwiftUI-native only — no
    WKWebView, no web cloning.
  - Adaptive: ScrollView + a centered max-width column (web PageContainer) that is regular on macOS/iPad
    and compact on iPhone; the hosted section's LazyVGrid(.adaptive) reflows the cards (ADR-002/006).

